<title>MOLDOVA: Moldovan 28-day T-bill yield rises, 91-day falls.</title>
<headline>Moldovan 28-day T-bill yield rises, 91-day falls.</headline>
<dateline>CHISINAU 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The yield on Moldovan 28-day Treasury bills rose to 29.32 percent annual from 26.60 percent at the previous auction last Tuesday, a National Bank official told Reuters.</p>
<p>91-day T-bills yielded 30.19 percent annual, compared to 32.05 percent at the previous auction last Tuesday.</p>
<p>Full details of the 28-day paper auction:</p>
<p>						Aug 28	  Aug 20</p>
<p>    Issue volume			  3.00 million lei  3.00 million lei</p>
<p>    Denominations			 1,000 lei     1,000 lei</p>
<p>    Nominal demand			2.11 million	6.38 million</p>
<p>    Volume sold			   2.11 million	3.00 million</p>
<p>    Yield				   29.32 pct     26.60 pct</p>
<p>    Price				   97.8 pct	98.0 pct</p>
<p>    Range of bids			 97.8-98.5 pct 97.7-98.5 pct</p>
<p>    Maturity				Sept 26, 1996 Sept 19, 1996</p>
<p>Full details of the 91-day paper auction:</p>
<p>    Issue volume			  7.00 million lei  10.00 million lei</p>
<p>    Denominations			 1,000 lei     1,000 lei</p>
<p>    Nominal demand			14.75 million     10.14 million</p>
<p>    Volume sold			   7.00 million	10.00 million</p>
<p>    Yield				   30.19 pct     32.05 pct</p>
<p>    Price				   93.0 pct	92.6 pct</p>
<p>    Range of bids			 92.5-94.0 pct 92.6-95.0 pct</p>
<p>    Maturity				Nov 28, 1996  Nov 21, 1996</p>
<p>--Dmitry Solovyov, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
